    "note": "A clean-room impact-feedback component on the Main Camera watches the reference enemy's collision-driven HitCount and, on its rising edge (a real Shooter3DProjectile trigger-collision, never input or a timer), opens a deterministic hit-stop window AND a decaying camera punch along WORLD +Z (the camera looks down +Z toward the enemy). World X/Y stay at rest, so the entire shake signal lives in Z. Both advance on Time.deltaTime (the fixture never alters Time.timeScale), so a pinned capture gives deterministic, capture-clock-aligned values. Samples copied verbatim from the raw bridge transcript; not synthesized."
  },
